<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus Hellenic net hit by special charge.</title>
<headline>Cyprus Hellenic net hit by special charge.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			   (In millions of pounds unless stated)</p>
<p>						   1996	    1995</p>
<p>    Operating profit			 8.51   vs     6.14</p>
<p>    Extraordinary item		     2.91   vs	nil</p>
<p>    Bad debts				  2.06   vs     1.38</p>
<p>    Pre-tax				    3.42   vs     4.76</p>
<p>    Net					  2.13   vs     3.37</p>
<p>    Dividend (15 cent)		     2.83   vs     1.91</p>
<p>    EPS  (in cents)			 12.5    vs     25.9</p>
<p>NOTE : The extraordinary item represents early retirement of 73 employees and costs incurred from the purchase of the Cyprus onshore operations of Barclays Bank PLC last April for 8.5 million pounds.</p>
<p>The results, which are preliminary, incorporate those of the on-shore operations of Barclays Bank from January 1, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
</text>
